{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>before Terach his father.</b> In his father's lifetime. And its midrash aggadah says: on account of his father he died — for Terach denounced his son Abram before Nimrod for smashing his idols, and he cast him into the fiery furnace. Haran was sitting and saying in his heart: if Abram prevails, I am of his; and if Nimrod prevails, I am of his. And when Abram was saved, they said to Haran: whose are you? Haran said to them: I am of Abram's. They cast him into the fiery furnace and he was burned — and this is 'Ur Kasdim' (Bereshit Rabbah). And Menachem explained אוּר as 'valley'; and so ״בָּאֻרִים כַּבְּדוּ אֶת ה׳״ (Isaiah 24), and likewise ״מְאוּרַת צִפְעוֹנִי״ (ibid. 11) — every hollow and deep cleft is called אוּר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:22.846604108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}